<title>USA: Clinton budget seeks fees for Surface Trans. Board.</title>
<headline>Clinton budget seeks fees for Surface Trans. Board.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>President Clinton's fiscal 1998 budget plan proposed assessing fees on railroads and shippers to completely offset expenses of the Surface Transportation Board.</p>
<p>The budget plan said the fees would be collected from those who benefit from continuation of functions of the Interstate Commerce Commission which were assumed by the STB, the ICC's successor.</p>
</text>
